01:43:02,608 --> 01:43:08,608
2012 is a 2009 American epic apocalyptic disaster film directed by Roland Emmerich, written by Emmerich and Harald Kloser, and
starring John Cusack, Chiwetel Ejiofor, Amanda Peet, Oliver Platt, Thandiwe Newton, Danny Glover, and Woody Harrelson.

16
01:49:54,782 --> 01:50:00,782
Based on the 2012 phenomenon, its plot follows numerous characters, including novelist Jackson Curtis (Cusack) and geologist Adrian Helmsley (Ejiofor), as
they struggle to survive an eschatological sequence of events including earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, megatsunamis, and a global flood.

17
01:56:46,956 --> 01:56:52,956
Filming, initially planned to take place in Los Angeles, began in
Vancouver in August 2008 and wrapped two months later.

18
02:03:39,130 --> 02:03:45,130
An extensive marketing campaign was launched for the film, which included the creation of a website from its main characters' point of view
and a viral marketing website on which filmgoers could register for a lottery number to save them from the ensuing disaster.

19
02:10:31,304 --> 02:10:37,304
Released in the United States by Sony Pictures Releasing on November 13, 2009, 2012 received mixed reviews, but was a commercial success,
grossing $791.2 million worldwide against a production budget of $200 million, becoming the fifth highest-grossing film of 2009.

20
02:17:23,478 --> 02:17:29,478
The film was nominated for Best Action, Adventure, or Thriller Film and Best Special Effects at the
36th Saturn Awards, and for Best Visual Effects at the 15th Critics' Choice Awards.

21
02:24:15,652 --> 02:24:21,652
The film explores themes of race against time, maya
civilization, civilization, natural disaster, earthquake.

22
02:31:07,826 --> 02:31:13,826
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
